# Vicky — the strong local brain behind Medusa's chat assistant (2026-09-17).
#
# Vicky used to be `claude -p --model sonnet` on the operator's metered Anthropic
# login. She is now Dolphin-Mistral-24B-Venice-Edition at Q8_0, on this machine,
# costing nothing per turn. The Claude engine still exists in medusa_vicky.py's
# ENGINES table but is disabled — one env var (ZYG_VICKY_CLAUDE=on) brings it
# back, and every Claude chat keeps its session id, so re-enabling resumes them.
#
# Why Q8_0 and not the usual Q4/Q6: this box's 4090 reports 49140 MiB, so the
# 25 GB of weights sit entirely in VRAM with room to spare for a 32k KV cache.
# The "generally unneeded" note on Q8 in the quant tables is written for 24 GB
# cards. Here the strong quant is free.
#
# Dense 24B, not an MoE like Victor's qwen3.6:35b-a3b — every token reads all
# 25 GB, so expect roughly a third of Victor's tokens per second. That is the
# trade that was accepted for the better brain.
#
# Deliberately NO `SYSTEM` line, for the same reason as Victor.Modelfile: the
# standing rules are read fresh from VICKY_RULES.md on every single turn
# (medusa_victor.system_prompt()). Baking them in here would freeze them at
# build time and an edit to the rules file would silently stop taking effect.
#
# Build with:  ollama create vicky -f config/Vicky.Modelfile
#
# FROM below is home-relative. Ollama does NOT expand `~`, so substitute the absolute
# path of your model store ($ZYG_MODELS_DIR, default ~/models) before building:
#   sed "s|^FROM ~|FROM $HOME|" config/Vicky.Modelfile | ollama create vicky -f -
FROM ~/models/gguf/Dolphin-Mistral-24B-Venice-Edition-Q8_0.gguf

# ── TEMPLATE: why this file has to carry one ─────────────────────────────────
# The first build of this model came out with `ollama show --template` printing
# `{{ .Prompt }}` and Capabilities listing `completion` alone — no `tools`. That
# is not Ollama being coy; it is Ollama failing to convert the template baked
# into the GGUF and falling back to raw completion, SILENTLY. Two separate
# reasons, both worth knowing before anyone "simplifies" this block away:
#
#  1. The GGUF's own Jinja template calls strftime_now("%Y-%m-%d"), an extension
#     Ollama's Go template engine does not implement. Conversion fails whole.
#  2. That template has NO tool support in the first place. It handles exactly
#     three roles and calls raise_exception() on anything else — Dolphin's
#     fine-tune shipped a simplified template in place of Mistral's tool-capable
#     one. So even a perfect conversion would have produced a model that cannot
#     be handed a tool schema.
#
# Left alone, the result is the worst kind of working: the model answers, fluent
# and confident, having been fed the raw transcript with no [INST] markers and
# no tools, and every image_* / video_* / run_bash call this app is built around
# silently becomes prose describing a call it never made.
#
# So the template below is Mistral v7 (tekken) written by hand, the format the
# BASE model — mistralai/Mistral-Small-24B-Instruct-2501 — was instruction-tuned
# on and whose tool tokens the weights still carry. Ollama infers the `tools`
# capability from the presence of .Tools here, and infers the parser for tool
# calls coming back from the literal `[TOOL_CALLS]` prefix, which is why that
# marker has to stay exactly as written.
#
# Tools are emitted immediately before the LAST user message, not at the top.
# That is Mistral's convention, not a stylistic choice — the model was trained
# with the schema in that position and moving it measurably degrades tool use.
#
# No <s> in the template: the GGUF sets add_bos_token, so Ollama's tokenizer
# adds BOS itself. Writing it here as well doubles it.
TEMPLATE """
{{- range $index, $_ := .Messages }}
{{- if eq .Role "system" }}[SYSTEM_PROMPT]{{ .Content }}[/SYSTEM_PROMPT]
{{- else if eq .Role "user" }}
{{- if and (le (len (slice $.Messages $index)) 2) $.Tools }}[AVAILABLE_TOOLS]{{ $.Tools }}[/AVAILABLE_TOOLS]
{{- end }}[INST]{{ .Content }}[/INST]
{{- else if eq .Role "assistant" }}
{{- if .Content }}{{ .Content }}
{{- if not (eq (len (slice $.Messages $index)) 1) }}</s>
{{- end }}
{{- else if .ToolCalls }}[TOOL_CALLS][
{{- range .ToolCalls }}{"name": "{{ .Function.Name }}", "arguments": {{ .Function.Arguments }}}
{{- end }}]</s>
{{- end }}
{{- else if eq .Role "tool" }}[TOOL_RESULTS]{"content": {{ .Content }}}[/TOOL_RESULTS]
{{- end }}
{{- end }}"""

# A tool loop replays the whole transcript every turn (Ollama has no session to
# resume), so the context holds a conversation plus tool results, not one
# question. 32k costs ~5 GB of KV here; there is headroom to raise it.
PARAMETER num_ctx 32768

# Mistral-Small-24B's own recommendation is a low temperature — it is noticeably
# more prone to drift at the 0.6 Victor uses than qwen is.
PARAMETER temperature 0.15
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
